<article class="env-lemma" id="01V7">
       
      
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01V7">Lemma <span data-tag="01V7">29.35.11</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Let $x \in X$ be a point. Let $V \subset S$ be an affine open neighbourhood of $f(x)$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The morphism $f$ is smooth at $x$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
There exists an affine open $U \subset X$, with $x \in U$ and $f(U) \subset V$ such that the induced morphism $f|_ U : U \to V$ is standard smooth. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Follows from the definitions and Algebra, Lemmas <a href="/tag/00T7" data-tag="00T7">10.137.6</a> and <a href="/tag/00TA" data-tag="00TA">10.137.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>